## Performance Trade-offs
Per-I/O sequence numbers add minimal overhead (8 bytes per operation) but provide strong correctness guarantees. The atomic operations introduce ~5-10ns latency per completion, which is negligible compared to NVMe access times (~100μs). However, under extreme burst conditions, contention on the completion ring indices can become a bottleneck, potentially requiring sharding or per-core completion queues.

